findings.finding:
(a) Every whole require is caught by the replay, but the grammar's value constraints are not pinned. No case changes under any of these hand mutants:
- re.match instead of fullmatch, which would admit 'rodata=off' through 'ro';
- selinux=[0-9] or enforcing=[0-9], which would admit selinux=0 and enforcing=0;
- lockdown=[a-z]+ or security=[a-z]+;
- any value for initrd=, console= or rootflags=, or loglevel=[0-9]+;
- dropping rw, rootfstype=, rootflags=, root=/dev/ or the PARTUUID/LABEL forms.
This is the same class as R4-2(a): the safety-relevant part (selinux=0, enforcing=0) has no vector.
(b) Legitimate entries refused. The initrd= class has no '+'. Debian 13's kernel-install layout puts '+' in every initrd path, because its kernel versions look like 6.12.x+deb13-amd64 (probe L01). Ubuntu's rootflags=subvol=@ and GRUB's BOOT_IMAGE= are also refused, but the loader is out of scope. W03 can avoid all three, or widen the grammar through review.

