questionAnswers.Q2:
Every v2 rule still holds.
- All 131 v2 negatives and 4 v2 accepted variants replay.
- R70 (schema enum), R71 (maxItems), L13 (parent rule first; V41 keeps the incomplete-census rule) and Q07 (reworded) refuse as the README says.
- Identity disjointness is subsumed: the 21 enum identities are pairwise distinct across components, and the KUBELET pattern matches none of them.
Legitimate hosts accepted:
- A05 to A08;
- C-d, a library shared by three native roles;
- S-c, a nested unpopulated leftover;
- I-b, the same inode number on another device;
- W4-c, a libssl outside the tree shared by SERVER and the gate;
- Fedora's rootflags=subvol=root, root=/dev/mapper/rhel-root, two console= words and a microcode initrd ahead of the main one.
Refusals by design: any quote; a library byte-identical to a tree file in a native-only role (R3-3); words outside the grammar (R5-4(b)).

questionAnswers.Q5:
Census and closure soundness are unchanged; the model diff touches only boot-entry rules.
Refused:
- a cgroup below a role cgroup (S-a), a nested leftover without its parent (S-d), a third broker child (S-f), a populated unenrolled leftover (S-g);
- a role-domain process outside its role cgroup (S-e), one inode for two files (I-a);
- content copies of another role's executable, by sha256 and verity or by sha256 alone (C-a, C-b, C-e);
- a file equal to the interpreter by verity (C-c);
- a gate library byte-identical to a tree file (W4-b).
I found no way for a bundle to carry its own observation of a foreign cgroup, process or program and qualify. No role can run another role's code or an interpreter's.
The stated residuals stand:
- interpreted scripts are declared, not observed;
- a Python runtime outside the tree;
- a fabricated unpopulated census entry with a matching count.
Beyond the vectors, the command-line probes G01 to G07, G09 and G11 to G13 are accepted (R5-1).

